        "filename": "Manitoulin Island swing bridge - Little Current, Ontario (2019).jpg",
        "caption": "Swing bridge between Manitoulin Island and the mainland, in Little Current, Ontario, was built in 1913 by the Algoma Eastern Railway.  Originally usable only by trains, it was modified in the late 1940s to allow road vehicles also to use it. The rail service was abandoned in the 1980s, and the tracks were removed in the 1990s. This view is from the southwest.",
